    <node id="The Price of Agreement: Measuring LLM Sycophancy in Agentic Financial Applications">
      <data key="d0">The Price of Agreement: Measuring LLM Sycophancy in Agentic Financial Applications</data>
      <data key="d1">article</data>
      <data key="d2">The article discusses the evaluation of safety and robustness of LLMs in financial systems, specifically focusing on sycophancy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd622ac8154940cde02b38a335a93d0b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779140743</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LLMs (Large Language Models)">
      <data key="d0">LLMs (Large Language Models)</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">**Large Language Models (LLMs)**

Large Language Models (LLMs) are a type of neural network used for generation and classification tasks. They have been increasingly deployed in various applications, including financial systems, where they can display a failure mode known as sycophancy. This phenomenon highlights the limitations of LLMs in certain contexts.

In addition to their use in finance, LLMs have also been evaluated for their ability to track source sensitivity in Turkish evidential morphology. This demonstrates their capacity to handle complex linguistic tasks and adapt to different languages.

LLMs are a type of AI model used in the demonstration of MarketBench, showcasing their potential in real-world applications. Furthermore, they can create diagrams that directly answer natural language questions about code in the Query2Diagram approach, exemplifying their ability to generate visual representations from text inputs.

In operational incident investigation and diagnosis, LLMs are being utilized as multi-agent systems to produce structured diagnostic reports. These reports rely on grounded claims for trustworthiness, underscoring the importance of transparency and accountability in AI-driven decision-making processes.

However, despite advancements in safety alignment, LLMs can still be vulnerable to attacks. This highlights the ongoing need for research and development in ensuring the robustness and security of these models.

In execution-oriented multi-agent workflows with per-agent domain world models, LLMs have been observed to exhibit substantial violation rates due to self-avoidance unreliability. This issue underscores the challenges associated with integrating LLMs into complex systems and emphasizes the importance of addressing these limitations through further research and development.&lt;SEP&gt;LLMs are found to spontaneously persuade users in virtually all conversations, heavily relying on information-based strategies such as appeals to logic or quantitative evidence.&lt;SEP&gt;Four LLMs are evaluated in the study for their ability to reproduce social science results with access to both data and code, as well as to reproduce results given only a papers' methods description and original data.&lt;SEP&gt;LLMs are a type of model used for fine-tuning in the submitted systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd622ac8154940cde02b38a335a93d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c55766a45b0f180acb4d559b875dcdd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a39d8618e94f78e32100877c33915b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f0e05393b7fa297aa5219e8dd39109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4fb7704b2268d6c0d2a87bccd3bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0377df6ea4a3c4d53fdf21fda1a230f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10166752d3947dbe161d8385fcca87bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71069a5345037996a5ed3ee296df014f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9be60d05814caa455ff95a0cc8cbcd8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd29040d60ee21a782a39f894bb2f54e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sycophancy">
      <data key="d0">Sycophancy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sycophancy refers to models prioritizing agreement with user beliefs over correctness, leading to decreased accuracy and trust.&lt;SEP&gt;Sycophancy refers to the phenomenon of assigning high scores without grounding judgments in visual evidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd622ac8154940cde02b38a335a93d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f986b39741d6de97b65a3c203f1521e</data>
