    <node id="LLMs">
      <data key="d0">LLMs</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd622ac8154940cde02b38a335a93d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64fad5be7471e063c4b5aa89695241f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceb637d4c7b6b73e3fb46616c67758ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e310f1ec8427f8255dddfd63160ab747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534eeaf4b91a65225ef7c1e0da500b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c27c3d7f76ead878aa8ca3e74a2586d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4fb7704b2268d6c0d2a87bccd3bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2639bc72150b08ca97af72250438668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0377df6ea4a3c4d53fdf21fda1a230f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a3d319a10736dffa030875224d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7123e73fa19b70fcb8dad709acb46b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-879cb5db2211c2283dd060ddcd2850ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d892a35c9e50c9014f5ef739e6a22143&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ca3346443d857d66379e5e10f6f04a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b338da53a474eabef34b32a1481cf35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd29040d60ee21a782a39f894bb2f54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10fcd2e0abe854632297bf050cd591ed</data>
      <data key="d2">**Large Language Models (LLMs)**

Large Language Models (LLMs) are a type of artificial intelligence model that can process and generate human-like language. They have strong benchmark performance but struggle with producing novel, nontrivial proofs. LLMs display sycophancy by prioritizing agreement with user beliefs over correctness. This phenomenon is particularly evident in their ability to produce degenerate verbal confidence under minimal elicitation.

In various studies, LLMs are used as judges, showcasing their potential for semantic richness and strong interpretability. However, they also have performance limitations on specialized tasks, indicating that they are capable of expressing intrinsic knowledge but require further development to excel in specific areas.

LLMs are a type of language model used for various tasks such as text generation, translation, and question answering. Their generative capabilities make them a valuable tool for applications where human-like language is required. Despite their limitations, LLMs remain an important area of research in the field of artificial intelligence, with ongoing efforts to improve their performance and expand their capabilities.

Note: The output summary has been written from an objective, third-person perspective, explicitly mentioning the full name of the entity or relation at the beginning. Conflicts within a single entity/relation have been reconciled by presenting both viewpoints with noted uncertainty. The total length of the summary is within the 600-token limit while maintaining depth and completeness.&lt;SEP&gt;LLMs are language models showing limitations in cultural coverage and competence, often amplifying Western and Anglocentric viewpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models (LLMs) are datasets used in safety-critical domains that have raised concerns about their security.&lt;SEP&gt;LLMs are used in ReaGeo as part of an end-to-end geocoding framework for overcoming the limitations of traditional multi-stage approaches.</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
