      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A smoothing kernel is used in FTN to bias the result toward spatial contiguity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141841</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="K-Winner-Take-All">
      <data key="d0">K-Winner-Take-All</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">K-winner-take-all is a procedure used in FTN to binarize the resulting group at a fixed capacity budget.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141841</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mixture-of-Experts">
      <data key="d0">Mixture-of-Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Mixture-of-experts is an approach that uses a high-dimensional, self-organizing binary mask over a large population of small but deep networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141845</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dendritic Models of Pyramidal Neurons">
      <data key="d0">Dendritic Models of Pyramidal Neurons</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dendritic models of pyramidal neurons are the inspiration behind the use of small but deep networks in FTN.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141845</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Synthetic Multi-Task Classification/Regression Generator">
      <data key="d0">Synthetic Multi-Task Classification/Regression Generator</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The synthetic multi-task classification/regression generator is a benchmark used to test FTN.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MNIST with Shuffled Class Labels">
      <data key="d0">MNIST with Shuffled Class Labels</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">MNIST with shuffled class labels is another benchmark used to test FTN, representing pure concept shift.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Permuted MNIST">
      <data key="d0">Permuted MNIST</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">Permuted MNIST is a third benchmark used to test FTN, representing domain shift.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779141854</data>
