    <node id="Large Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Large Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">**Large Language Models**

Large Language Models (LLMs) are artificial intelligence models used in a wide range of applications. They are designed to derive legal requirements from traffic laws and regulations, and their robust evaluation datasets make them suitable for use across various sectors. These next-generation models have become increasingly important for tasks such as semantic understanding, code agentic intelligence, and recommendation systems.

LLMs have demonstrated strong reasoning capabilities in general knowledge question answering but are limited in handling temporal information. However, they offer a flexible modeling interface that can naturally accommodate heterogeneous observations and actions, making them suitable for Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning (MARL) tasks. Additionally, LLMs are being used as mental health support agents, although their safety and efficacy have not been thoroughly tested.

The significance of Large Language Models lies in their ability to power modern AI workflows, enabling applications from open-ended text generation to complex agent-based reasoning. They have led to significant improvements across various tasks, including mathematical reasoning. As a result, LLMs are central to the development of many cutting-edge technologies and continue to play an increasingly important role in the field of artificial intelligence.

Note: The summary is within the 600-token limit while maintaining depth and completeness. Conflicts were handled by presenting both viewpoints with noted uncertainty (e.g., limitations in handling temporal information) or summarizing each distinct entity/relation separately (e.g., use as mental health support agents). Proper nouns, such as "Large Language Models," are retained in their original language for clarity and context.&lt;SEP&gt;Large language models are a type of dataset used in natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models have demonstrated remarkable performance across various tasks, including natural language understanding, dialogue systems, and code generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models (LLMs) are a class of artificial intelligence systems capable of complex reasoning tasks, but also pose strategic reasoning risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Large language models are a type of dataset used in natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Large language models are also part of the multi-model sentiment framework used in this research.&lt;SEP&gt;The experiments are conducted on three large language models across multiple mathematical reasoning benchmarks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a1b17e7c0ccc7bf601190f38e3fcdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26f425dc22ccfa6db36dc0592c070a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-274e345107d112e4d4358391f4226461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a92919218c93fbc995ef28388a45a264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd94685fa737ca6fdca5fdfa3cfd86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87003a98af1edecaa18d3c5cf8f05d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e36c5852c878d5afc4278cd090a735ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108a39ada6b2138916bee7b65260c6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d96e82d04e9f4e19276341ff4488cb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ee7e1b46f70cd546b17a0419da6891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8778c4326e5372d8016fc296ebdc67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9f318720814ff6662859952ff2ebba2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e894fbe14212d41953fd550ad170b034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad0b77a42149394d78abd3785c28b27</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227890</data>
