    <node id="KV Cache">
      <data key="d0">KV Cache</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The KV cache is a critical component of many attention mechanisms, storing key-value pairs for efficient lookup and computation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-274e345107d112e4d4358391f4226461</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779148245</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GQA">
      <data key="d0">GQA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">GQA (head-level compression) is an existing solution that reduces the KV cache per layer but still maintains a linear relationship between the KV cache and sequence length.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-274e345107d112e4d4358391f4226461</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779148245</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MLA">
      <data key="d0">MLA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MLA (embedding dimension-level compression) is another existing solution that compresses the embedding dimension to reduce KV cache size.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-274e345107d112e4d4358391f4226461</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779148250</data>
