    <node id="Aligning with Your Own Voice: Self-Corrected Preference Learning for Hallucination Mitigation in LVLMs">
      <data key="d0">Aligning with Your Own Voice: Self-Corrected Preference Learning for Hallucination Mitigation in LVLMs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper "Aligning with Your Own Voice: Self-Corrected Preference Learning for Hallucination Mitigation in LVLMs" presents a framework to address hallucinations in Large Vision-Language Models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large Vision-Language Models (LVLMs)">
      <data key="d0">Large Vision-Language Models (LVLMs)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">LVLMs are models that suffer from hallucinations, which can be mitigated using the proposed framework.&lt;SEP&gt;LVLMs are systems that combine vision and language capabilities, but remain vulnerable to hallucinations.&lt;SEP&gt;LVLMs are advanced models requiring precise local region-based reasoning grounded in actual visual evidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ba0f324a606c4227526581aeedb047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cfa4cdeb2d8dae52b2c64ae56623799</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779225649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Existing Preference Learning-Based Approaches">
      <data key="d0">Existing Preference Learning-Based Approaches</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Existing approaches rely on proprietary models to construct preference datasets, introducing a distributional mismatch between the proprietary and target models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149181</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alignment via VErified Self-correction DPO (AVES-DPO)">
      <data key="d0">Alignment via VErified Self-correction DPO (AVES-DPO)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">AVES-DPO is a framework that aligns LVLMs using in-distribution data derived from the model's intrinsic knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149181</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intrinsic Knowledge">
      <data key="d0">Intrinsic Knowledge</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The model's intrinsic knowledge is used to derive in-distribution data for alignment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149185</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Consensus-Based Verification Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Consensus-Based Verification Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A consensus-based verification mechanism diagnoses diverse hallucinations and guides the model to self-correct.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149185</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hallucination Mitigation">
      <data key="d0">Hallucination Mitigation</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The goal of AVES-DPO is to mitigate hallucinations in LVLMs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05a4ca61ae3ed284142fb22c23657755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779149189</data>
