    <node id="Diffusion Models">
      <data key="d0">Diffusion Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Diffusion models are a type of deep learning model used for image generation tasks, which can be controlled using controllable diffusion methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion models are generative models that offer promising learning-based solutions for chip placement but have limitations such as requiring long sampling times and often resulting in overlaps due to their dependence on gradient-based solvers during the sampling process.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion models are central to modern generative modeling, balancing memorization and generalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion Models are a type of deep-learning model used for image and video processing tasks, including super-resolution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f36584a3c17d75781a357f1a3e17848d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a66eda0565fcf4309a0c1f0cc86b80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d464c49d9f37f044c3d86a74bbeddf57</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779213420</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
