    <node id="Reinforcement Learning (RL)">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning (RL)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reinforcement Learning (RL) is a machine learning technique used to train VLMs for enhanced reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;RL is a machine learning paradigm for training agents to make decisions in complex environments by interacting with them through trial and error.&lt;SEP&gt;RL is a machine learning method used for training models to make decisions based on rewards or penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;RL optimizes policies for reward but imposes few constraints on how decisions evolve over time, leading to temporally incoherent behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee6a8292ee988e4d64c218b75e3c5f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8227fa84b33ba6c4091b7e5804332bdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44784699c64a5aec415cf1e1bb031fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505d76e0ef7c1c2d1377c1c2c9d16f54</data>
