    <node id="Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">**Reinforcement Learning**

Reinforcement learning is an optimization technique used to train models based on rewards or penalties for their actions. It is an approach used for training agents to make decisions in complex environments, where the algorithm learns through trial and error by interacting with an environment and receiving rewards for desired actions.

This method is particularly useful for automating dispatching rules, but existing models often struggle with scalability issues. However, reinforcement learning overcomes the limitations of classical controllers by leveraging shared representations to enable efficient adaptation across tasks and environments.

Reinforcement learning also formalizes feedback uncertainty using its framework. Furthermore, it has been applied in various contexts, such as optimizing the generation accuracy of ReaGeo using a distance-deviation-based reward.

In essence, reinforcement learning is a type of machine learning that uses information unavailable during execution to retrospectively generate training signals. This approach enables agents to make decisions in complex environments and adapt efficiently across tasks and environments, making it a valuable tool for various applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-245522d5b100e4d1a221b34fd4f3a20d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-806e6e5aef8defe7ecaeafa8c2ceb771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a47d5248e3997970eb290095468c98a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b513da659cdd3445e4c3872d13a21d07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c940b0f6301bc2033a8a1954c70de79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe7fc82733330af762752cd6e70c474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b76d2c6d9d5022e82c584d66a9027c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10fcd2e0abe854632297bf050cd591ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226821</data>
