    <node id="Model Context Protocol (MCP)">
      <data key="d0">Model Context Protocol (MCP)</data>
      <data key="d1">protocol</data>
      <data key="d2">The Model Context Protocol is used by the Auditor to dynamically inspect the target dataset and produce a yes/no verdict.&lt;SEP&gt;The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is a common interface for connecting large language model (LLM) agents to external tools, but its reliance on stateless, eager schema injection imposes a hidden per-turn overhead the MCP Tax or Tools Tax.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-92ae3699975fb22408181c1b3b3cd1ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa8f729dd44bf86d6178016c1edf568</data>
