    <node id="Vision-Language-Action (VLA) Models">
      <data key="d0">Vision-Language-Action (VLA) Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">VLA models have strong zero-shot generalization capabilities but require cloud-based deployment due to massive parameter sizes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157506</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cloud-Based Deployment">
      <data key="d0">Cloud-Based Deployment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cloud-based deployment introduces network jitter and inference latency, which can induce spatiotemporal misalignment in mobile navigation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AsyncShield Framework">
      <data key="d0">AsyncShield Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The AsyncShield framework discards traditional black-box time-series prediction in favor of a deterministic physical white-box spatial mapping to address the issue of spatiotemporal misalignment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temporal Pose Buffer">
      <data key="d0">Temporal Pose Buffer</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">The temporal pose buffer is used by the system to accurately convert temporal lag into spatial pose offsets and restore the VLA's original geometric intent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157517</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kinematic Transformations">
      <data key="d0">Kinematic Transformations</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">Kinematic transformations are utilized by the system to maintain a temporal pose buffer and accurately convert temporal lag into spatial pose offsets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157517</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PPO-Lagrangian Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">PPO-Lagrangian Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The PPO-Lagrangian algorithm is used to solve the constrained Markov decision process (CMDP) formulated for edge adaptation, which balances intent restoration fidelity and physical safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047ce2bc252a55d9055c31539d3a7c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157522</data>
