    </node>
    <node id="Kullback-Leibler Divergence">
      <data key="d0">Kullback-Leibler Divergence</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">The Kullback-Leibler divergence is a metric used in the Kerimov-Alekberli model, governed by a dynamic threshold derived from the Fisher Information Metric.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d10488f697007297062eb31177c84c90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157753</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fisher Information Metric">
      <data key="d0">Fisher Information Metric</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fisher Information Metric is a concept used to derive a dynamic threshold for the Kullback-Leibler divergence in the Kerimov-Alekberli model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d10488f697007297062eb31177c84c90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157757</data>
