    <node id="Large (Vision-)Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Large (Vision-)Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Large (vision-)language models are AI systems that can process and understand human language, but remain susceptible to jailbreaking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779157943</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GPT-5">
      <data key="d0">GPT-5</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">GPT-5 is a frontier model developed by OpenAI that has shifted from refusal-based safeguards to safe completion.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a large language model used as a baseline in experiments comparing its performance to that of MTRouter.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a model that consumes significantly fewer tokens than Kimi-K2 and Claude-Sonnet-4.5 on the same tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 degrades by -1.8 pp when using self-correction.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is another type of VLM that only responds with text when answering questions about images.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a large language model that serves as a baseline for comparison in numerical reasoning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b12fa74b99bde4b11a0b2ee0662b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c628da8f1a15116206f1eeae72db4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f031cdaecf3a806d1ce1ffc191c8d256&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db73b95d2d4357d5595446b233ad0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40018c67d794720f4d500c856e412b79</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779223425</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Claude-Sonnet-4.5">
      <data key="d0">Claude-Sonnet-4.5</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Claude-Sonnet-4.5 is another frontier model that was tested against the novel multi-turn jailbreaking method.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude-Sonnet-4.5 is another frontier LLM analyzed in this study, consuming over 1.5 million more tokens than GPT-5 on average.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c628da8f1a15116206f1eeae72db4cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779196036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Jailbreaking Method">
      <data key="d0">Jailbreaking Method</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The novel multi-turn jailbreaking method exploits the vulnerability of safe completion in frontier models by simulating benign-seeming intentions and exploiting consistency properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
