      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The LLM-Augmented Traffic Signal Control Framework is a proposed method for traffic signal control that integrates LSTM-based short-term traffic state prediction, predictive phase selection, structured large language model reasoning, and safety-constrained action filtering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5afcc78472e920445d94dd9f10ec59ab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779165849</data>
