      <data key="d0">LLM-as-a-Judge</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LLM-as-a-Judge is a large vision-language model used in Agri-CPJ to select the stronger response from complementary viewpoints based on domain-specific criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM-as-a-Judge is a paradigm for evaluating language model outputs that exhibits systematic biases compromising evaluation reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM-as-a-Judge is an approach in automated evaluation systems that plays critical roles in model alignment, leaderboard construction, quality control, and so on.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6e66d4e85d142173cf1ea9e9a149cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a057fb1f41ab14090c349549bfb86b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-879cb5db2211c2283dd060ddcd2850ac</data>
