    <node id="Dialogue-Style Sequence Prediction Problem">
      <data key="d0">Dialogue-Style Sequence Prediction Problem</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The DLM formulates multi-agent decision making as a dialogue-style sequence prediction problem under the centralized training with decentralized execution paradigm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dd94685fa737ca6fdca5fdfa3cfd86c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Centralized Training with Decentralized Execution Paradigm">
      <data key="d0">Centralized Training with Decentralized Execution Paradigm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The DLM uses the centralized training with decentralized execution paradigm to train agents in a unified manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dd94685fa737ca6fdca5fdfa3cfd86c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Supervised Fine-Tuning Phase">
      <data key="d0">Supervised Fine-Tuning Phase</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The supervised fine-tuning phase of the DLM leverages dialogue-style datasets for centralized training with inter-agent context and generates executable actions from offline trajectories.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dd94685fa737ca6fdca5fdfa3cfd86c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Group Relative Policy Optimization Phase">
      <data key="d0">Group Relative Policy Optimization Phase</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The group relative policy optimization phase enhances robustness to out-of-distribution actions through lightweight reward functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dd94685fa737ca6fdca5fdfa3cfd86c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="On the Memorization of Consistency Distillation for Diffusion Models">
      <data key="d0">On the Memorization of Consistency Distillation for Diffusion Models</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper "On the Memorization of Consistency Distillation for Diffusion Models" is a research study on diffusion models and their memorization behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Consistency Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Consistency Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Consistency distillation is a framework for improving the memorization-generalization trade-off in diffusion models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Teacher Model">
      <data key="d0">Teacher Model</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">The teacher model has memorized data and serves as a representative example for analyzing consistency distillation's impact on memorization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Student Model">
      <data key="d0">Student Model</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">The student model is trained using consistency distillation, which reduces transferred memorization while preserving sample quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177182</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Random Feature Neural Network Model">
      <data key="d0">Random Feature Neural Network Model</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A random feature neural network model [Bonnaire et al., 2025] is used to theoretically analyze the behavior of consistency distillation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177182</data>
