    </node>
    <node id="Mixed-Radix Hyperbolic Rotation CORDIC (MR-HRC)">
      <data key="d0">Mixed-Radix Hyperbolic Rotation CORDIC (MR-HRC)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The MR-HRC algorithm is a modified mixed-radix hyperbolic rotation CORDIC combining radix-2 and radix-4 iterations for efficient hardware implementation of the sigmoid function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e63184f8475817efd492ed80ef98cb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177351</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hyperbolic Tangent Function">
      <data key="d0">Hyperbolic Tangent Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Hyperbolic tangent function is mathematically related to the sigmoid function, enabling a reduced range computation that improves convergence behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e63184f8475817efd492ed80ef98cb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177351</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radix-2 Linear Vectoring CORDIC (R2-LVC)">
      <data key="d0">Radix-2 Linear Vectoring CORDIC (R2-LVC)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The R2-LVC algorithm computes the hyperbolic tangent by dividing hyperbolic sine and cosine values derived from the MR-HRC algorithm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e63184f8475817efd492ed80ef98cb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779177356</data>
      <data key="d6" />
