      <data key="d0">MNIST Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">MNIST is a dataset used to evaluate the proposed approach's performance in handling permanent, temporal, and overlapping disagreement patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;MNIST is a dataset used for image recognition and classification tasks, achieving 95.89% accuracy with the proposed approach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a46b0909fa6d0ef55b6d73270c41134</data>
