      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186312</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Explainability">
      <data key="d0">Explainability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Explainability refers to the ability of an agent to provide causal explanations for its actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Explainability refers to the ability to provide clear and understandable reasons for the decisions made by an argumentation framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7283e187a29957165bf39353160ea1b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8116cd69ada8e9cc2054f7f3401cf253</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779195322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Partially Observable Markov Decision Process (POMDP)">
      <data key="d0">Partially Observable Markov Decision Process (POMDP)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A POMDP is a mathematical framework used to model decision-making in partially observable environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7283e187a29957165bf39353160ea1b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Variational Framework">
      <data key="d0">Variational Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The variational framework is a method for instantiating the criteria of intentionality, rationality, and explainability as an agentic action chain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7283e187a29957165bf39353160ea1b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T-Maze Paradigm">
      <data key="d0">T-Maze Paradigm</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The T-maze paradigm is a canonical dataset used to evaluate the performance of agents in navigating complex environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7283e187a29957165bf39353160ea1b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186320</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Empowerment">
      <data key="d0">Empowerment</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Empowerment is an operational metric that measures the channel capacity between actions and anticipated observations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7283e187a29957165bf39353160ea1b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186320</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="From Similarity to Structure: Training-free LLM Context Compression with Hybrid Graph Priors">
      <data key="d0">From Similarity to Structure: Training-free LLM Context Compression with Hybrid Graph Priors</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper "From Similarity to Structure: Training-free LLL Context Compression with Hybrid Graph Priors" proposes a training-free and model-agnostic compression framework for long-context large language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186475</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Long-Context Large Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Long-Context Large Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Long-Context Large Language Models are computationally expensive to run and often fail to reliably process very long inputs, making context compression an important component of many systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186475</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Training-Free Compression Framework">
      <data key="d0">Training-Free Compression Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed framework is a training-free and model-agnostic compression method that selects a compact set of sentences guided by structural graph priors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186482</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hybrid Sentence Graph">
      <data key="d0">Hybrid Sentence Graph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A hybrid sentence graph combines mutual k-NN semantic edges with short-range sequential edges to guide the selection of compact sentences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186482</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topic Skeleton">
      <data key="d0">Topic Skeleton</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The topic skeleton is extracted via clustering, representing a condensed version of the input text's topics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186486</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Task Relevance Score">
      <data key="d0">Task Relevance Score</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">A score that integrates task relevance, cluster representativeness, bridge centrality, and cycle coverage cue to rank sentences for compression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186486</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Budgeted Greedy Selection with Redundancy Suppression">
      <data key="d0">Budgeted Greedy Selection with Redundancy Suppression</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A budgeted greedy selection method that produces a readable compressed context in original order by suppressing redundancy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186490</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="From Similarity to Structure: Training-free LLL Context Compression with Hybrid Graph Priors">
      <data key="d0">From Similarity to Structure: Training-free LLL Context Compression with Hybrid Graph Priors</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6c3d3ee7936b859072a3ee9ad3a5562</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper addresses the problem of computationally expensive long-context large language models and proposes a training-free compression framework.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186493</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PDF Visual Element Parsing Framework">
      <data key="d0">PDF Visual Element Parsing Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The PDF Visual Element Parsing Framework is a lightweight and production-ready solution for extracting visual elements from PDF documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186625</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)">
      <data key="d0">Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is an approach that combines multimodal retrieval with augmented generation to improve document understanding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186625</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PDF Documents">
      <data key="d0">PDF Documents</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">PDF documents contain critical visual elements such as figures, tables, and forms whose accurate extraction is essential for document understanding and multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spatial Heuristics">
      <data key="d0">Spatial Heuristics</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed solution uses a combination of spatial heuristics to accurately detect visual elements in PDF documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layout Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Layout Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed solution also employs layout analysis to associate captions with their corresponding visual elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Similarity">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Similarity</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed solution uses semantic similarity to further improve the accuracy of caption association.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MMDocRAG Benchmark">
      <data key="d0">MMDocRAG Benchmark</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The MMDocRAG benchmark is a dataset used to evaluate the performance of multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4a07398a3eb380d303c65471a3f5b4a</data>
