    <node id="Cycle Adversarial Prompt Optimization Framework">
      <data key="d0">Cycle Adversarial Prompt Optimization Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cycle Adversarial Prompt optimization framework is designed to improve both CoT reasoning accuracy and stability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e65899f92452776d1e2d8e56956888d2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186891</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Forward Solver">
      <data key="d0">Forward Solver</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">A forward solver generates candidate reasoning chains in each cycle of the CAP-CoT framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e65899f92452776d1e2d8e56956888d2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186898</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Challenger">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Challenger</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">An adversarial challenger constructs plausible but deliberately flawed chains using targeted error strategies in the CAP-CoT framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e65899f92452776d1e2d8e56956888d2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186900</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Feedback Agent">
      <data key="d0">Feedback Agent</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">A feedback agent contrasts the two chains and produces step-aligned structured feedback in the CAP-CoT framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e65899f92452776d1e2d8e56956888d2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779186902</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Users' Input Prompt">
      <data key="d0">Users' Input Prompt</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The users' input prompt is open-ended and often does not follow proper syntactic rules, creating ambiguous queries that yield multiple interpretations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0733197acf40fb64366f709d6d6f836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779187027</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prompt Disambiguation Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Prompt Disambiguation Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">We propose a pre-inference prompt optimization mechanism via explicit prompt disambiguation to address the limitation of prior works.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0733197acf40fb64366f709d6d6f836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779187034</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Risks">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">We identify semantic risks in the prompt, which are checked for multi-perspective consistency and resolved to prevent semantic conflicts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0733197acf40fb64366f709d6d6f836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779187034</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LLM Inference Process">
      <data key="d0">LLM Inference Process</data>
      <data key="d1">process</data>
      <data key="d2">Our method explicitly resolves semantic ambiguity, producing a more focused attention distribution to semantically essential tokens without disturbing the internal mechanism of LLM inference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0733197acf40fb64366f709d6d6f836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779187038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
