      <data key="d0">Paired Discrepancy Enlargement</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Paired discrepancy enlargement is a technique used in ArmSSL for verification, enforcing feature-space orthogonality between clean and watermark counterparts to produce a reliable verification signal against the suspect model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199199</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Latent Representation Entanglement">
      <data key="d0">Latent Representation Entanglement</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Latent representation entanglement is a component of ArmSSL that integrates with distribution alignment to suppress OOD clustering, avoiding dense clusters of watermark samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199204</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distribution Alignment">
      <data key="d0">Distribution Alignment</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distribution alignment in ArmSSL minimizes the distributional discrepancy between watermark and clean representations, disguising watermark samples as natural in-distribution data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199204</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reference-Guided Watermark Tuning Strategy">
      <data key="d0">Reference-Guided Watermark Tuning Strategy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">This strategy allows the watermark to be learned as a small side task without affecting the main task by aligning watermarked encoder outputs with those of the original clean encoder on normal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199208</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Controllable Spoken Dialogue Generation">
      <data key="d0">Controllable Spoken Dialogue Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Controllable Spoken Dialogue Generation is an LLM-driven grading system for K-12 non-native English learners.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199359</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="China's National Curriculum (CSE)">
      <data key="d0">China's National Curriculum (CSE)</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">China's National Curriculum is used as a representative case for adapting LLM outputs to learner abilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199366</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DDPO Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">DDPO Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The DDPO algorithm is a multi-turn GRPO-based approach designed to preserve dialogue diversity while holistically optimizing dialogue quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199366</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Graded Vocabulary Lists">
      <data key="d0">Graded Vocabulary Lists</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">Graded vocabulary lists are part of the comprehensive suite of new resources provided by the framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199370</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Turn Dialogue Corpus">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Turn Dialogue Corpus</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The multi-turn dialogue corpus is another resource provided by the framework to support precise control over lexical complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199370</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="K-12 Non-Native English Learners">
      <data key="d0">K-12 Non-Native English Learners</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">K-12 non-native English learners are the target audience for the Controllable Spoken Dialogue Generation system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34c5de08734f1ccb57ec06429af892b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199374</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="On the Properties of Feature Attribution for Supervised Contrastive Learning">
      <data key="d0">On the Properties of Feature Attribution for Supervised Contrastive Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">This paper explores feature attribution explanations for supervised contrastive learning in neural networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neural Networks (NNs)">
      <data key="d0">Neural Networks (NNs)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Neural networks are a type of machine learning model used for classification tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrastive Learning (CL)">
      <data key="d0">Contrastive Learning (CL)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrastive learning is an approach to training neural networks that focuses on creating an embedding space where similar data points are pulled together and dissimilar data points are pushed apart.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199519</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Supervised Contrastive Learning (SCL)">
      <data key="d0">Supervised Contrastive Learning (SCL)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Supervised contrastive learning uses labels as similarity criteria to create an embedding space with well-clustered projected data points.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199524</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Robustness">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Robustness</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial robustness refers to a model's ability to resist attacks that aim to mislead the model into making incorrect predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199524</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Out-of-Distribution Detection">
      <data key="d0">Out-of-Distribution Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Out-of-distribution detection is the ability of a model to identify when it is being asked to make predictions on data points outside its training distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199528</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Feature Attribution Explanations">
      <data key="d0">Feature Attribution Explanations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Feature attribution explanations provide insights into how a neural network makes predictions based on input features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e4bebf7715af2c9d1047938049edd28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779199528</data>
      <data key="d6" />
