      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Adaptive decoupled moment routing is a technique that routes modified gradients only to the first moment while preserving magnitude-faithful second-moment statistics, and it was found to consistently avoid collapse across methods, optimizers, and scale.</data>
