    <node id="BLAST">
      <data key="d0">BLAST</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">BLAST is a benchmarking methodology and associated dataset for evaluating the accuracy of Large Language Models (LLMs) in generating Answer Set Programming (ASP) code.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42ee7e1b46f70cd546b17a0419da6891</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779203532</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Answer Set Programming">
      <data key="d0">Answer Set Programming</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Answer Set Programming is a declarative paradigm that has received less attention in the context of LLMs.&lt;SEP&gt;The prototype system implements core components of the approach using answer set programming, ensuring polynomial-time data complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Answer set programming is a method for handling inconsistent prioritized data, which has been extended with quantifiers in ASP(Q).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42ee7e1b46f70cd546b17a0419da6891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa8db6b063cab5b2b36b29bd40793c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4ffff9ba5dac98a07aac47ac8e0de46</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220294</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ASP Code Generation">
      <data key="d0">ASP Code Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">ASP code generation is one of the tasks evaluated by BLAST.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42ee7e1b46f70cd546b17a0419da6891</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779203539</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
