    </node>
    <node id="Patch Tokens">
      <data key="d0">Patch Tokens</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Patch tokens are intermediate representations that are aligned with anchor vectors in SAGA-ReID.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a45bf678ca7078a36ca306ecefdd317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206628</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Global Pooling">
      <data key="d0">Global Pooling</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Global pooling is an aggregation mechanism used in CLIP-based methods, which aggregates spatial features into a single global token.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a45bf678ca7078a36ca306ecefdd317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ResRank">
      <data key="d0">ResRank</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">ResRank employs an Encoder-LLM to compress each candidate passage into a single embedding, which is then fed alongside the query text into a Reranker-LLM for listwise ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;ResRank is a unified retrieval-reranking framework that addresses challenges in large language model based listwise reranking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206787</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multimodal LLMs">
      <data key="d0">Multimodal LLMs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multimodal LLMs project visual inputs into compact token representations, inspiring ResRank's compression mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206787</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Encoder-LLM">
      <data key="d0">Encoder-LLM</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Encoder-LLM compresses each candidate passage into a single embedding for listwise ranking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206794</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reranker-LLM">
      <data key="d0">Reranker-LLM</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Reranker-LLM is used alongside the query text to perform listwise ranking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206794</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Residual Connection Structure">
      <data key="d0">Residual Connection Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A residual connection structure combines encoder embeddings with contextualized hidden states from the reranker to alleviate misalignment between representation spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206798</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cosine-Similarity-Based Scoring Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Cosine-Similarity-Based Scoring Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The scoring mechanism uses one-step cosine-similarity-based scoring, eliminating autoregressive decoding and generation bottlenecks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779206798</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
