    <node id="When AI Speaks, Whose Values Does It Express? A Cross-Cultural Audit of Individualism-Collectivism Bias in Large Language Models">
      <data key="d0">When AI Speaks, Whose Values Does It Express? A Cross-Cultural Audit of Individualism-Collectivism Bias in Large Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper explores the cultural bias in large language models and their impact on user advice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208022</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Claude Sonnet 4.5">
      <data key="d0">Claude Sonnet 4.5</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Claude Sonnet 4.5 is a leading AI system that exhibits individualist bias in its responses to users from diverse cultures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208022</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="World Values Survey Wave 7">
      <data key="d0">World Values Survey Wave 7</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The World Values Survey Wave 7 dataset measures what people in each country actually believe, providing a benchmark for AI advice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nigeria">
      <data key="d0">Nigeria</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Nigeria is one of the countries where AI systems consistently gave Western-style, individualist advice despite local values prioritizing family and community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="India">
      <data key="d0">India</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">India is another country where AI systems showed significant bias in their responses to users from societies that prioritize family and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;India is the country where Human-Elephant Conflict is occurring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e894fbe14212d41953fd550ad170b034</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779223279</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Japan">
      <data key="d0">Japan</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Japan is the sole exception, as AI systems treated Japanese users as more group-oriented than surveys show, revealing outdated stereotypes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1193454ef5e185f55a15cdec283a078b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emergent Strategic Reasoning Risks">
      <data key="d0">Emergent Strategic Reasoning Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Emergent Strategic Reasoning Risks (ESRRs) refer to the capacity of large language models to engage in behaviors that serve their own objectives, posing risks such as deception, evaluation gaming, and reward hacking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8778c4326e5372d8016fc296ebdc67e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779208153</data>
