    <node id="Rethinking Publication: A Certification Framework for AI-Enabled Research">
      <data key="d0">Rethinking Publication: A Certification Framework for AI-Enabled Research</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper proposes a certification framework for AI-enabled research, addressing the publication system's limitations in handling pipeline-generated work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211235</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AI Research Pipelines">
      <data key="d0">AI Research Pipelines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">AI research pipelines produce a growing share of publishable academic output, including work meeting existing peer-review standards for quality and novelty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211235</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Publication System">
      <data key="d0">Publication System</data>
      <data key="d1">system</data>
      <data key="d2">The publication system was built on the assumption of universal human authorship and lacks a principled way to evaluate knowledge produced through automated pipelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211242</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Two-Layer Certification Framework">
      <data key="d0">Two-Layer Certification Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The framework separates knowledge quality assessment from grading of human contribution, allowing publication systems to handle pipeline-generated work consistently and transparently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211242</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Normative-Conceptual Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Normative-Conceptual Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper uses normative-conceptual analysis for framework design under four explicit constraints.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211247</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Framework Design">
      <data key="d0">Framework Design</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The framework grades contributions as Category A (pipeline-reachable), Category B (requiring human direction at identifiable stages), and Category C (beyond current pipeline reach at the formulation stage).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211247</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Benchmark Slots">
      <data key="d0">Benchmark Slots</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The framework introduces benchmark slots for fully disclosed automated research as both a transparent publication track and a calibration instrument for reviewer judgment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211251</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contribution Grading">
      <data key="d0">Contribution Grading</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Contribution grading is contemporaneous, based on pipeline capability at the time of submission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211251</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dry-Run Validation">
      <data key="d0">Dry-Run Validation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The framework can certify knowledge appropriately while tolerating irreducible attribution uncertainty, as shown by dry-run validation on two representative submission cases spanning key attribution scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f92416ce1ab40a1abd7e32f118a086c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779211255</data>
      <data key="d6" />
