    </node>
    <node id="Router Initialization Trap">
      <data key="d0">Router Initialization Trap</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The router initialization trap refers to a phenomenon where the model fails to escape a shallow equilibrium after ~2 steps at initialization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad110990ca6cc9a17e5632b94fa3fe51</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212276</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Task Optimization over Networks of Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Task Optimization over Networks of Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-Task Optimization over Networks of Tasks is a powerful approach for solving multiple tasks in parallel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MONET">
      <data key="d0">MONET</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MONET is a multi-task optimization algorithm that models the task space as a graph to enable knowledge transfer between tasks and exploit the topology of the task space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MAP-Elites">
      <data key="d0">MAP-Elites</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MAP-Elites is an existing multi-task optimization approach that relies on a fixed, discretized archive and disregards the topology of the task space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Population-based Methods">
      <data key="d0">Population-based Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Population-based methods are a type of multi-task optimization algorithm that scale poorly for large task sets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Task Space Graph">
      <data key="d0">Task Space Graph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The task space graph is a representation of the task space as a graph, where tasks are nodes and edges connect tasks in the task parameter space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212405</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Social Learning">
      <data key="d0">Social Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Social learning generates candidates from neighboring nodes via crossover in MONET.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212405</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Individual Learning">
      <data key="d0">Individual Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Individual learning refines a node's own solution independently via mutation in MONET.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b50eb193d4b7beed74fdee062999a545</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212410</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
