    <node id="Seeing Fast and Slow: Learning the Flow of Time in Videos">
      <data key="d0">Seeing Fast and Slow: Learning the Flow of Time in Videos</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper "Seeing Fast and Slow: Learning the Flow of Time in Videos" is a research study on perceiving and controlling the passage of time in videos.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Time">
      <data key="d0">Time</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Time is studied as a learnable visual concept, enabling models to reason about and manipulate its flow in videos.&lt;SEP&gt;Time is a fundamental concept in understanding the behavior of distributed AI inference systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80cbb950ef117c5df6a16610100445d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Videos">
      <data key="d0">Videos</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">Videos are central to modern computer vision research, with the passage of time being a key aspect to consider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temporal Super-Resolution">
      <data key="d0">Temporal Super-Resolution</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Temporal super-resolution transforms low-FPS, blurry videos into high-FPS sequences with fine-grained temporal details.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Speed-Conditioned Video Generation">
      <data key="d0">Speed-Conditioned Video Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">This model produces motion at specified playback speed by generating videos at different speeds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temporal Forensics Detection">
      <data key="d0">Temporal Forensics Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">Temporal forensics detection involves identifying whether a video has been sped up or slowed down.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-095492fc4bcb8832760d86b5dfbd65ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Read the Paper, Write the Code: Agentic Reproduction of Social-Science Results">
      <data key="d0">Read the Paper, Write the Code: Agentic Reproduction of Social-Science Results</data>
      <data key="d1">paper</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper discusses an agentic reproduction system that extracts structured methods descriptions from papers and reproduces results without access to original code or data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212834</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agentic Reproduction System">
      <data key="d0">Agentic Reproduction System</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The agentic reproduction system extracts structured methods descriptions from papers, runs reimplementations under strict information isolation, and enables deterministic comparison of reproduced outputs to the original results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212841</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Structured Methods Descriptions">
      <data key="d0">Structured Methods Descriptions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Structured methods descriptions are extracted from papers by the agentic reproduction system for reproducing results without access to original code or data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212841</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Deterministic Comparison">
      <data key="d0">Deterministic Comparison</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The agentic reproduction system enables deterministic comparison of reproduced outputs to the original results, allowing for accurate evaluation of agent performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212845</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Error Attribution Step">
      <data key="d0">Error Attribution Step</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An error attribution step is used in the agentic reproduction system to trace discrepancies through the system chain and identify root causes of failures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779212845</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agent Scaffolds">
      <data key="d0">Agent Scaffolds</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Agent scaffolds are used in the study to evaluate agent performance on reproducing results given only a paper's methods description and original data.&lt;SEP&gt;Agent scaffolds are used in agentic AIs to implement human-developed plans during software development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00d7716eae39c6d5a5594bf34114050e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b2afb905e3ac712e2c9231fdfc39c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779217406</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HalluScope">
      <data key="d0">HalluScope</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">HalluScope is a benchmark designed to understand the extent of hallucinations in LVLMs.</data>
