    <node id="Process Supervision via Verbal Critique Improves Reasoning in Large Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Process Supervision via Verbal Critique Improves Reasoning in Large Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Process Supervision via Verbal Critique Improves Reasoning in Large Language Models is a research paper that explores the use of verbal critique to improve reasoning in large language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4a5a929bdfb09229babed8e9871f5e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220113</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inference-time scaling for LLM reasoning">
      <data key="d0">Inference-time scaling for LLM reasoning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Inference-time scaling for LLM reasoning refers to the process of improving the performance of large language models during inference time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4a5a929bdfb09229babed8e9871f5e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220113</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chain depth, sample breadth, and learned step-scorers (PRMs)">
      <data key="d0">Chain depth, sample breadth, and learned step-scorers (PRMs)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chain depth, sample breadth, and learned step-scorers (PRMs) are three axes that have been previously explored for improving LLM reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4a5a929bdfb09229babed8e9871f5e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220120</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Verbal Process Supervision (VPS)">
      <data key="d0">Verbal Process Supervision (VPS)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Verbal Process Supervision (VPS) is a training-free framework that uses structured natural-language critique from a stronger supervisor to guide an iterative generate-critique-refine loop up to a round budget R.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4a5a929bdfb09229babed8e9871f5e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220120</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GPT-5.4 (High), GPT-5.4 (Low)">
      <data key="d0">GPT-5.4 (High), GPT-5.4 (Low)</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">GPT-5.4 (High) and GPT-5.4 (Low) are two versions of the GPT-5 model used in the experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4a5a929bdfb09229babed8e9871f5e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779220124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
