    <node id="From Noise to Intent: Anchoring Generative VLA Policies with Residual Bridges">
      <data key="d0">From Noise to Intent: Anchoring Generative VLA Policies with Residual Bridges</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The paper "From Noise to Intent: Anchoring Generative VLA Policies with Residual Bridges" presents a novel approach to bridging high-level semantic understanding and low-level physical control in embodied intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bridging High-Level Semantic Understanding with Low-Level Physical Control">
      <data key="d0">Bridging High-Level Semantic Understanding with Low-Level Physical Control</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bridging high-level semantic understanding with low-level physical control is a persistent challenge in embodied intelligence due to the spatiotemporal scale mismatch between cognition and action.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Generative VLA Policies">
      <data key="d0">Generative VLA Policies</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Generative VLA policies typically adopt a "Generation-from-Noise" paradigm, which disregards the disparity between high-level semantic understanding and low-level physical control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226039</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ResVLA">
      <data key="d0">ResVLA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">ResVLA is an architecture that shifts the paradigm to "Refinement-from-Intent," utilizing spectral analysis to decouple control into a deterministic low-frequency anchor and a stochastic high-frequency residual.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226039</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spectral Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Spectral Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Spectral analysis is used in ResVLA to decouple control into a deterministic low-frequency anchor and a stochastic high-frequency residual.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Residual Diffusion Bridge">
      <data key="d0">Residual Diffusion Bridge</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The residual diffusion bridge is a component of ResVLA that focuses on refining local dynamics via a residual diffusion process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184da693de71f9b2b2481b01afaf1e16</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779226044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
