    <node id="Vision--language models (VLMs)">
      <data key="d0">Vision--language models (VLMs)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Vision-language models (VLMs) are deep learning architectures designed to process both visual and textual inputs, but often struggle with abstract visual reasoning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bongard-LOGO">
      <data key="d0">Bongard-LOGO</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">Bongard-LOGO is a synthetic benchmark of abstract concept learning that provides ground-truth generative programs for evaluating vision-language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Componential--Grammatical (C--G) paradigm">
      <data key="d0">Componential--Grammatical (C--G) paradigm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Componential-Grammatical (C-G) paradigm reformulates Bongard-LOGO as a symbolic reasoning task based on LOGO-style action programs or structured descriptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large language models (LLMs)">
      <data key="d0">Large language models (LLMs)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Large language models (LLMs) are pre-trained language models that can be fine-tuned for specific tasks, and in this case, achieve large gains when given symbolic inputs derived from images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LOGO-style action programs">
      <data key="d0">LOGO-style action programs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">LOGO-style action programs are a type of structured description used in the Componential-Grammatical (C-G) paradigm to represent abstract concepts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1779227178</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Evaluating AI Meeting Summaries with a Reusable Cross-Domain Pipeline">
