    <edge source="Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs)" target="CNSL-bench Dataset">
      <data key="d7">4.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The CNSL-bench dataset supports fine-grained analysis of key manual articulatory forms, including air-writing, finger-spelling, and the Chinese manual-alphabet.&lt;SEP&gt;The CNSL-bench dataset is used to evaluate the performance of MLLMs in sign language understanding across multiple input modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The CNSL-bench dataset is used to evaluate the instruction-following robustness of MLLMs in sign language understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Our results reveal that current MLLMs remain substantially inferior to human performance in sign language understanding.</data>
